        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5647c3bf-843c-54f5-ac10-48721433b134",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes, Hal Stalmaster\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California\n- Parks and Attractions: Magic Kingdom, Disneyland Park, Splash Mountain, Tokyo Disneyland, Walt Disney World Resort\n- Films and Books: Johnny Tremain, Song of the South\n- Topics: American Revolution, Disney characters, fairy tales\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the children's novel \"Johnny Tremain,\" which won the 1944 Newbery Medal.\n- The 1946 Disney film \"Song of the South\" provided the characters, stories, and songs that inspired Splash Mountain.\n- \"Johnny Tremain\" is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions and based on Esther Forbes's novel of the same name.\n- The 1957 film \"Johnny Tremain\" retells events in Boston, Massachusetts, before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Hal Stalmaster, born Harry Lapidus Stalmaster on March 29, 1940, is an American former actor known for the lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film \"Johnny Tremain.\"\n- Walt Disney initialized Magic Kingdom, and WED Enterprises designed it.\n- Magic Kingdom's layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, and the park is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\n- Splash Mountain is a log flume dark ride operating at Disneyland, Tokyo Disneyland, and the Magic Kingdom at Walt Disney World Resort.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "98eb933a-1f6a-5a79-a291-42494d88387b",
        "text": "Page: Johnny Tremain (film). Sentence: Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions, based on the 1944 Newbery Medal-winning children's novel of the same name by Esther Forbes, retelling the story of the years in Boston, Massachusetts prior to the outbreak of the American Revolution.\nPage: Magic Kingdom. Sentence: Initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, its layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, and is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\nPage: Hal Stalmaster. Sentence: Harry Lapidus Stalmaster, known as Hal Stalmaster (born March 29, 1940), is an American former actor, known for his lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film of the American Revolution \"Johnny Tremain\", based on the 1943 Esther Forbes novel of the same name.\nPage: Splash Mountain. Sentence: Splash Mountain is a log flume dark ride at Disneyland, Tokyo Disneyland, and the Magic Kingdom at the Walt Disney World Resort, based on the characters, stories, and songs from the 1946 Disney film \"Song of the South\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
